  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is the primary purpose of each term in a PID controller (Proportional, Integral, Derivative)? (5 marks)', 'Proportional: produces an output proportional to the present error, giving a quick corrective action and reducing rise time, but alone it leaves a steady-state error. Integral: accumulates the error over time, removing steady-state error, though too much causes overshoot and oscillation. Derivative: responds to the rate of change of the error, anticipating future error, adding damping, reducing overshoot and improving stability.', null, '[{"point": "P: output proportional to present error - faster response, reduces error but leaves offset", "marks": 2}, {"point": "I: sums past error - eliminates steady-state error (may add overshoot)", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "D: reacts to rate of change - damping, reduces overshoot, improves stability", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
