  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'A transmission line with characteristic impedance Z₀ = 50 Ω is terminated with a load Z_L = 100 + j50 Ω. What is the value of the normalised load impedance? If you were to use a single-stub tuner, would you place a shorted or open stub? Why? (5 marks)', 'Normalised load impedance z_L = Z_L/Z₀ = (100 + j50)/50 = 2 + j1. A short-circuited stub is usually preferred: a shorted end is easy to make exactly, does not radiate, and has no fringing capacitance, so its reactance is predictable and stable; an open end radiates and has end effects (although open stubs are convenient in microstrip circuits). The stub length is chosen from the Smith chart to cancel the susceptance at the point where the real part of the admittance is 1.', null, '[{"point": "z_L = Z_L/Z₀ = 2 + j1", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Shorted stub preferred", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Reasons: no radiation/fringing from the open end, easier to realise and adjust, stable; (open stub possible in microstrip)", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
