What kind of network data should be collected for training AI models? (20 marks)', 'Collect: radio measurements (RSRP, RSRQ, SINR, CQI, timing advance) and call records showing drops and failed handovers; traffic and load data per cell (PRB utilisation, throughput, number of active users, latency, packet loss) over time; network configuration, neighbour lists and topology; alarms, fault and maintenance logs; contextual data such as time of day, location, events and weather; and customer experience indicators (complaints, app QoE). Data must be cleaned, time-synchronised, labelled (e.g. drop/no-drop) and anonymised to protect subscriber privacy.', null, '[{"point": "Radio KPIs: RSRP, RSRQ, SINR, CQI, handover success/failure, call drop records", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Traffic and load: PRB utilisation, throughput, active users, time-of-day/location patterns", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Configuration, alarms/fault logs, topology, weather/events, user experience data", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Data quality, labelling, privacy and anonymisation", "marks": 3}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
