  values ('ME', 'passage', 'CASE I: AI in Telecommunications
A mobile network operator wants to reduce call drops and improve Quality of Service (QoS) using AI/ML solutions.

How can AI be used to predict network congestion and reroute traffic in real time? (15 marks)', 'Train time-series and machine-learning models (e.g. LSTM, gradient boosting) on historical load to forecast congestion per cell minutes or hours ahead, and anomaly-detection models to spot unusual drops. When congestion is predicted, a self-organising network (SON) or SDN controller acts automatically: adjusts handover thresholds and antenna tilt, steers users to less-loaded cells or frequency bands (load balancing), offloads to Wi-Fi, reroutes backhaul traffic, or prioritises voice. Reinforcement learning can learn the best actions; results are monitored in a closed loop.', null, '[{"point": "Forecasting models (time-series, LSTM, gradient boosting) on cell load to predict congestion ahead", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Anomaly detection and classification of drop causes", "marks": 3}, {"point": "Automated actions: load balancing, handover parameter tuning, traffic steering, SON, SDN rerouting, reinforcement learning", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Closed loop with monitoring", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
