  values ('ME', 'passage', 'CASE I: AI in Telecommunications
A mobile network operator wants to reduce call drops and improve Quality of Service (QoS) using AI/ML solutions.

Discuss trade-offs between centralised cloud AI and edge AI in telecom applications. (15 marks)', 'Centralised cloud AI has large computing power, sees the whole network and is easier to train and update, but adds latency, needs heavy backhaul bandwidth, raises data-privacy concerns and fails if the link is lost. Edge AI (at base stations or MEC servers) decides in milliseconds for real-time functions such as handover and scheduling, reduces backhaul traffic and keeps data local, but has limited compute and storage, smaller models and is harder to manage across many sites. A hybrid approach - train in the cloud, deploy lightweight models at the edge, federated learning - balances both.', null, '[{"point": "Cloud AI: large compute and data, global view, easier model training/updating; but latency, bandwidth cost, privacy, dependence on backhaul", "marks": 7}, {"point": "Edge AI: low latency real-time decisions, less backhaul, privacy, resilience; but limited compute, harder management, smaller models", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Hybrid: train in cloud, infer at edge", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
