  values ('ME', 'passage', 'CASE II: Satellite Internet for Remote Areas
An ISP is exploring Low Earth Orbit (LEO) satellites to provide internet in remote mountainous regions.

Compare the pros and cons of LEO satellite internet versus terrestrial fixed wireless. (20 marks)', 'LEO satellite internet: covers remote valleys and high mountains without building ground infrastructure, can be deployed quickly, latency (20-50 ms) far better than geostationary satellites, and is resilient to local disasters. Cons: expensive terminals and subscriptions for rural users, capacity shared in each cell, sensitivity to obstructions (trees, mountains) and heavy rain, dependence on foreign operators and licensing/data-sovereignty issues. Terrestrial fixed wireless: lower cost per user, local control, high capacity and easy upgrades; but needs towers with line-of-sight and power, which is hard and costly in Bhutan''s mountainous terrain, and has limited range.', null, '[{"point": "LEO pros: coverage anywhere incl. mountains, quick deployment, low latency vs GEO, no terrain line-of-sight need", "marks": 7}, {"point": "LEO cons: terminal cost, subscription, weather/obstruction, capacity sharing, regulatory/sovereignty, dependence on foreign operator", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Fixed wireless pros/cons: cheaper per user, local control, high capacity; but needs towers, line-of-sight, difficult terrain, power", "marks": 7}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
